@!internal
module nupp.runtime.bitops

--[[
What a bitwise operator lowers to on a target without one.

`a & b` compiles to `a & b` on LuaJIT and to a call on this module under
`--dialect lua51`, so a program reaches it by writing the operator rather than
by naming it. On a host with the native provider it *is* LuaJIT's `bit`; on
stock Lua it is the scalar fallback beneath
[](nupp.runtime.services.contracts.BitopsProvider), which answers to the same
names and signatures.

Every operand is normalized to a signed 32-bit word first, so a wider integer
has to be split into limbs by whoever holds it.
]]

const contracts = require("nupp.runtime.services.contracts")

export = contracts.bitops:assemble(function(): contracts.BitopsProvider
    local native = contracts.bitops:lookup("nupp.native")
    if native ~= nil then
        return native
    end

    return require("nupp.runtime.provider.scalarbitops")
end)
